  "pairing": {
    "note": "The cyber and physical blocks of a segment have different row counts and no sample-level correspondence. Any two-view experiment must choose a pairing rule; the loader requires that choice to be named rather than defaulted. The ratios below are what a rule has to bridge.",
    "timestamp_note": "fdi_physical.csv has no timestamp column at all -- its first column is `mid`. Pairing that block with its cyber block by time is therefore not possible even in principle, whatever rule is chosen. A user of the IEEE DataPort mirror raised exactly this in 2024-07 and received no reply.",
